&lt;strong&gt;&lt;p&gt;D. Other&lt;&sol;p&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After examining the available medical evidence, the Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services determines that no national coverage determination is appropriate at this time. Section 1862(a)(1)(A) of the Social Security Act decisions should be made by local Medicare Administrative Contractors through a local coverage determination process or case-by-case adjudication. See Heckler v. Ringer, 466 U.S. 602, 617 (1984) (Recognizing that the Secretary has discretion to either establish a generally applicable rule or to allow individual adjudication.). See also, 68 Fed. Reg. 63692, 63693 (November 7, 2003).&lt;&sol;p&gt;
